(1930975, 263284, 14386, '<td valign="top">LOL....for those who commented about a woman standing somewhere, you''re right.  I took a lot of shots along with this shot and this is one of them.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=266269" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/14386/thumb/266269.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/14386/thumb/266269.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/14386/thumb/266269.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Anyway...Sally helped me set up this shot.During lunchbreak in school, I requested a friend to sharpen the pencils, I laid them down on the floor (with a black velvet cloth as a base), then asked Warren (and later on Sally) to arrange them in the same manner as shown in the box of the Prismacolors pencil.  Not an original idea.  But I really went down on the floor to take the shot.  Unlike the box picture which was taken from the top, I experimented on the DOF and the angle.  An dthe rest is history.<br/> <br/>Many thanks for the votes.  <br/> <br/>Manny<br/> <br/></td>', 'LOL....for those who commented about a woman standing somewhere, you''re right.  I took a lot of shots along with this shot and this is one of them.   Anyway...Sally helped me set up this shot.During lunchbreak in school, I requested a friend to sharpen the pencils, I laid them down on the floor (with a black velvet cloth as a base), then asked Warren (and later on Sally) to arrange them in the same manner as shown in the box of the Prismacolors pencil.  Not an original idea.  But I really went down on the floor to take the shot.  Unlike the box picture which was taken from the top, I experimented on the DOF and the angle.  An dthe rest is history. Many thanks for the votes.   Manny ', '2005-12-07 08:22:48.000000', NULL, 0),
