(1931122, 263284, 17203, '<td valign="top">Two days ago, my wife and I were discussing the ribbon standings, and I pointed out that I might have an advantage because none of the current challenges were suited to portraiture. So not only did you prove me completely wrong, you did it with a well-deserved blue and a 7+ score. ROFL!<br/> <br/>Now if you''ll excuse me, I have to go torture some kittens or something. ;-)</td>', 'Two days ago, my wife and I were discussing the ribbon standings, and I pointed out that I might have an advantage because none of the current challenges were suited to portraiture. So not only did you prove me completely wrong, you did it with a well-deserved blue and a 7+ score. ROFL! Now if you''ll excuse me, I have to go torture some kittens or something. ;-)', '2005-12-07 09:28:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1931131, 263643, 19744, '<td valign="top">Dear Brennan, rated 10 I thought it would do much better. It is not only showing a collection but also gives a good message. Brave composition where I''m only not sure on the very light background. Otherwise light/shadows give lige to the picture. Very well done. Yours, Jan</td>', 'Dear Brennan, rated 10 I thought it would do much better. It is not only showing a collection but also gives a good message. Brave composition where I''m only not sure on the very light background. Otherwise light/shadows give lige to the picture. Very well done. Yours, Jan', '2005-12-07 09:30:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1931146, 263284, 14386, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by scalvert:</b></div><hr/><i> Two days ago, my wife and I were discussing the ribbon standings, and I pointed out that I might have an advantage because none of the current challenges were suited to portraiture. So not only did you prove me completely wrong, you did it with a well-deserved blue and a 7+ score. ROFL!<br/> <br/>Now if you''ll excuse me, I have to go torture some kittens or something. ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Shannon, I was just lucky.  I don''t have your creativity and imagination.  Mine is just a copy from a box cover.  But yours are always original.  And you have the record of not leaving the dpchallenge''s homepage for how many weeks now?  Anyway...I think we inspire each other.</td>', 'Originally posted by scalvert: Two days ago, my wife and I were discussing the ribbon standings, and I pointed out that I might have an advantage because none of the current challenges were suited to portraiture. So not only did you prove me completely wrong, you did it with a well-deserved blue and a 7+ score. ROFL! Now if you''ll excuse me, I have to go torture some kittens or something. ;-)   Shannon, I was just lucky.  I don''t have your creativity and imagination.  Mine is just a copy from a box cover.  But yours are always original.  And you have the record of not leaving the dpchallenge''s homepage for how many weeks now?  Anyway...I think we inspire each other.', '2005-12-07 09:36:21.000000', NULL, 0),
